cadence projects edit: missing --if-match, --body

usage: cadence projects edit --project PROJECT --if-match IF_MATCH [--dry-run] --body JSON

Rename or re-describe a project (PATCH /projects/{p}, operation projects.edit)

Rename or re-describe a project. Send ifMatch with the etag (or rev) of your last projects.get; a
stale revision fails with precondition-failed and the current revision to re-read.

Flags:
  --project            Project slug [required]
  --if-match           The revision the change is based on (the ETag of the last read); a mismatch answers 412 with currentRev [required]
  --dry-run            Validate and report what would happen without changing anything [boolean; default false]

Body (--body JSON, --body @file or --body @- for standard input; required):
  description          (string)
  name                 (string)

A command: an Idempotency-Key is generated for each call; --dry-run shows the result without a change.

Global flags:
  --url URL               control plane (env CADENCE_URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8080; /api is appended)
  --token TOKEN           API key, sent as a Bearer token (env CADENCE_TOKEN; create one with credentials new)
  --idempotency-key KEY   commands only: reuse a key to replay a command's first result (default: a new key)
  -h, --help              this command's flags
